{aligned}{∮}_{C}x{y}^{2}\\,dx+2{x}^{2}y\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(4xy-2xy)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2xy\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the region $D$ can be represented in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 6,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe change of variables formula for plane polar coordinates states that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our double integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2xy\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}2\\cdot r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}2{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,{\\int }_{0}^{6}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406426 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406427 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406426 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406428 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406426 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406429 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406426 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406430 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406426 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406431 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406426 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406426 1077 "selection" 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406426 1079 #edb/ref 17592186406431 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406426 1080 #uuid "18f53d24-ffcb-51fb-8ef8-920f533f7ad1" 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406427 1081 "r-{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )" 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406427 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406427 1