l surface $f(x,y,z)=0.$  \n\nA normal vector to the level surface that passes through the point $(0,0,2)$ can be found by computing $∇f(0,0,2).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(0,0,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}-1)i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}-1)j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}-1)k \\\\  & =2x\\text{ }i+\\frac{2y}{9}\\text{ }j+\\frac{z}{2}\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇f(0,0,2) & =2(0)\\text{ }i+\\frac{2(0)}{9}\\text{ }j+\\frac{(2)}{2}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =k \\\\  & =⟨0,0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, the vector form of the equation of the line that is parallel to $∇f(0,0,2)$ and passes through the point $(0,0,2)$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,2⟩+t\\,∇f(0,0,2)=⟨0,\\,0,\\,2⟩+t\\,⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406522 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406523 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406522 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406524 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406522 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406525 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406522 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406526 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406522 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406527 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406522 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406522 1077 "selection" 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406522 1079 #edb/ref 17592186406524 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406522 1080 #uuid "fa0a835b-df77-526f-b20f-c5410f491aab" 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406523 1081 "⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩+t\\,⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406523 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406523 1084 #uuid "124556c0-f467-5318-900e-7da585d6554e" 13194139533507 17592186045585 t