 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $B$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entries of its first two rows are in columns $3$ and $2,$ respectively (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ has a coefficient matrix that is **not** in row echelon form." 13194139533508 17592186405019 true] [17592186406535 1074 "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since ${b}_{22}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ is **not** in row echelon form." 13194139533508 17592186405019 false] [17592186406535 1074 "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since ${b}_{22}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ is **not** in row echelon form." 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406536 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406537 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406536 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406538 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406536 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406539 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406536 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406540 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406536 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406541 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406536 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406536 1077 "selection" 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406536 1079 #edb/ref 17592186406541 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406536 1080 #uuid "cca85be9-de3b-5573-9094-83fec95f1da6" 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406537 1081 "$A$ and $C$ only" 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406537 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406537 1084 #uuid "9415a6bc-b845-5416-a630-c09cf1de4075" 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406538 1081 "$A$ only" 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406538 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406538 1084