lity symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the car's displacement *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=kt.\n$$" 13194139533508 17592186405019 true] [17592186406549 1074 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The rate of growth of a **car's displacement** $D(t)$ **increases** at a **rate** that's **proportional** to the **time** $t$ since the car started moving.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *car's displacement* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *interval of time* since the car started moving. In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}∝t.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the car's displacement *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=kt.\n$$" 13194139533508 17592186405019 false] [17592186406549 1074 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The rate of growth of a **car's displacement** $D(t)$ **increases** at a **rate** that's **proportional** to the **time** $t$ since the car started moving.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *car's displacement* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *interval of time* since the car started moving. In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}∝t.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the car's displacement *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=kt.\n$$" 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406550 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406551 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406550 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406552 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406550 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406553 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406550 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406554 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406550 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406555 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406550 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406550 1077 "selection" 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406550 1079 #edb/ref 17592186406551 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406550 1080 #uuid "46d988ad-b19d-531c-8043-d4cc3d8d9aff" 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406551 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=kt,\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406551 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406551 1084 #uuid "78f2fba8-448d-54b0-9f0b-a7a12167cb79" 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406552 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=kD,\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406552 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406552 1084 #uuid "81d0803a-89e6-5850-b97e-24717c7d2073" 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406553 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{kt}{D},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406553 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406553 1084 #uuid "a3657738-9337-52ad-bf3f-63b326fd491f" 13194139533507 17592186045585 true] [17592186406554 1081 "\\frac{\\t